Task: dispatch-refactor-impl (plan agui_hitl_interrupts_a1f3c2d8, phase P2)

Why: spec FR3 and the P3 emission work both need to treat 'this call
produces an interrupt' as a question separate from 'emit this interrupt'.
The old code fused them in an if on toolconfirmation.FunctionCallName.

Changes (agui/internal/stream/processor.go):
- New interruptCallHandler type and interruptCallHandlers map, holding
  the adk_request_confirmation entry.
- ProcessEvent's FunctionCall branch now looks up the handler instead of
  comparing names.
- The TODO(non-tool-interrupts) comment moved from the branch to the
  table, which is where the next call name gets registered.
- Reason literal replaced with interrupt.ReasonToolCall.
- Local 'interrupt' variable renamed to 'intr' to stop it shadowing the
  package of the same name.

Deliberately NOT done here:
- No 'callName' key added to the emitted adk metadata. Adding one would
  change the tool_call wire and break spec acceptance criterion 6.
  Record.CallName already falls back to toolconfirmation.FunctionCallName
  when absent, which is exactly why that fallback exists. P3 sets
  callName only for adk_request_input.
- The handler still returns immediately on the first interrupt. Scanning
  all parts is the next todo (multi-interrupt), kept separate so this
  change stays provably behaviour preserving.

Verification: TestConfirmationInterruptWireBaseline passes unchanged, so
the emitted stream is byte identical modulo timestamps. go fmt, go vet,
CI=true go test ./... all clean.
